  "body": "## What changed\n\nThis PR adds a first slice of a HEIDENHAIN Klartext (`.H`) reader to `camcraft-gcode`.\n\n- New entry points: `parse_klartext(program)` and `parse_klartext_with(program, &KlartextOptions)`. The output is the same `ParsedProgram` / `ParsedSection` / `cl::Toolpath` as the RS-274 reader gives.\n- New module `crates/gcode/src/klartext/` (7 files, each below 400 lines). It uses the section builder, the arc resolver, the numeric domain checks and the peck bound of the RS-274 reader.\n- `ParsedSection` gets a `tool_name: Option<String>` field. A named `TOOL CALL \"FLAT-6\"` has no tool number. Without the field, two named tools would merge into one section. The RS-274 reader sets `None`.\n- Decision record: `docs/decisions/2227-klartext-reader.md`.\n\n### The reader reads\n\n- `BEGIN PGM <name> MM` and `END PGM` (the names must agree; a missing `END PGM` is refused as a truncated program).\n- `BLK FORM 0.1 Z` / `0.2` (checked; not part of the toolpath).\n- `TOOL CALL` with a tool number or a `\"NAME\"`, axis Z, `S`, `F` (`DL` / `DR` only when zero). `TOOL DEF` (no effect).\n- `L` with `X Y Z`, `IX IY IZ`, `R0`, modal `F`, and `FMAX` for one block only.\n- `CC` (both axes or none), `C` with `DR+` / `DR-` (a full circle gives two arcs), `CR` with `R+` / `R-`, and `CT` (tangent to the previous element).\n- `CYCL DEF 247` (preset `Q339` 1 to 6, read as work offset G54 to G59).\n- `CYCL DEF 200`, `203`, `205`, called by `CYCL CALL` or `M99`. Each infeed goes `Q202` deeper from the surface `Q203`. The tool ends at the higher of the two set-up clearances. Each call records a `cl::Cycle`.\n- `FN 0: Qn = <literal>`, `Qn = <literal>`, and Q references in values (`X+Q1`, `X-Q1`).\n- `STOP`, `;` comments, `*` structure blocks, `~` continuation lines.\n- M functions 0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 8, 9, 13, 14, 30, 99, 137, and `M140 MB MAX` / `M140 MB <n>`. `M140 MB MAX` needs `KlartextOptions::tool_axis_max_z`, because the end of the traverse range is a machine value.\n\n### The reader refuses (by name, with the line; the message starts with `block N:`)\n\n`RND`, `CHF`, `LP`, `CP`, `CTP`, `APPR`, `DEP`, FK blocks, `LBL`, `CALL`, `RL`, `RR`, axes other than X/Y/Z, polar words, `FAUTO` / `FU` / `FZ`, `M91`, `M92`, `M89`, `M136` and other M functions, `FN` other than `FN 0`, Q formulas, `BEGIN PGM ... INCH`, a tool axis other than Z, a helix (arc with a Z change), old-style cycles (`CYCL DEF 1.0`), cycles other than 200 / 203 / 205 / 247, `CYCL CALL PAT` / `POS`, and the cycle options that change the motion when they are not zero (`Q210`, `Q212`, `Q213`, `Q257`, `Q379`, `Q395`). The decision record gives the reason for each.\n\n## Tests\n\nNew test binary `crates/gcode/tests/klartext` (25 tests). Pinning tests:\n\nReason for the new top-level test binary: `tests/parse/` is the suite of the RS-274 reader; Klartext is a different input language with its own entry point (`parse_klartext`), so it gets its own directory suite. `camcraft-gcode` then has two small test binaries.\n\n\n- `klartext_post_golden_reads_back_into_the_stream_motion`: the recorded Klartext post golden (`crates/post/tests/recorded/golden/heidenhain-klartext/picomax.nc`) reads back into the motion of its CL stream (`crates/post/tests/klartext/contour.cnc`): points, rapid or feed, feeds, arc centres and directions. It also checks tool, rpm, preset, stops and the line map across the continuation line.\n- `klartext_post_golden_needs_the_traverse_end_for_m140`.\n- Review fix: `klartext_stop_with_m0_or_m1_records_one_program_stop` (a `STOP M0` or `STOP M1` block records one `ProgramStop`, not two stops).\n- Paths: `klartext_fmax_is_blockwise_and_f_is_modal`, `klartext_incremental_words_and_literal_q_parameters`, `klartext_cc_and_c_arcs_with_both_directions_and_a_full_circle`, `klartext_cr_radius_sign_picks_the_minor_or_major_arc`, `klartext_ct_continues_the_tangent_of_the_previous_element`, `klartext_tool_calls_by_number_and_name_split_sections`, `klartext_m_functions_set_spindle_coolant_and_stops`.\n- Cycles: `klartext_cycle_200_pecks_from_the_surface_and_ends_at_the_2nd_clearance`, `klartext_cycles_203_and_205_without_chip_breaking_drill_at_cycl_call`, `klartext_cycle_247_selects_the_preset_as_work_offset`, `klartext_unsupported_cycles_and_cycle_options_are_refused_by_name`, `klartext_invalid_cycle_definitions_and_calls_are_refused`.\n- Refusals: `klartext_functions_outside_the_slice_are_refused_by_name_and_block` (17 functions, line and block number), `klartext_inch_programs_and_unknown_words_are_refused`, `klartext_program_frame_is_checked`, `klartext_arc_preconditions_are_refused`, `klartext_m140_mb_max_needs_the_traverse_end`.\n- Degenerate input (each run on a worker thread with a time limit; a panic or a hang fails): `klartext_every_truncation_of_the_golden_is_refused_without_a_panic` (each prefix before `END PGM`), `klartext_bad_numbers_are_refused` (22 cases), `klartext_huge_programs_parse_or_refuse_in_time` (200 000 blocks, a 1 MB block, 100 000 continuation lines), `klartext_seeded_mutations_of_the_golden_never_panic` (3000 seeded mutations), `klartext_empty_and_comment_only_input_is_refused`.\n\n## Gate results (head 6482595d3, Windows lane `winbuild`, `CAMCRAFT_GATE_JOBS=6`)\n\n| Step | Result |\n|---|---|\n| `cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/main`: gcode build | ok (8 s) |\n| gcode suites: lib | ok |\n| gcode suites: klartext (24 tests) | ok |\n| gcode suites: parse (37 tests, RS-274 reader) | ok |\n| `cargo clippy -p camcraft-gcode --all-targets -- -D warnings` | ok |\n| `cargo xtask gate heavy --base origin/main --dry-run` | the diff reaches no heavy lane |\n| Light lane | not reached: no light twin covers `camcraft-gcode` |\n\nThe quick plan has no `camcraft-app` or `camcraft-ui` step (no crate depends on `camcraft-gcode`). Thus no Mac run was necessary. The known red `ui` lib test (#4322) is not in this plan.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- No real TNC-written program was read. The hand-written test programs follow the public manual syntax. Only one recorded program golden of our own post exists.\n- No app command, MCP tool or CLI verb reads `.H` files yet. `camcraft-gcode` has no consumer. This PR adds no user-facing command, so no MCP tool is necessary.\n- `CYCL DEF 206` / `207` (tapping), `LBL` calls, `RND` / `CHF`, polar and inch programs stay open on #2227.\n\nChangelog: camcraft-gcode reads a first slice of HEIDENHAIN Klartext (.H) programs (lines, CC/C/CR/CT arcs, tool calls, presets and drilling cycles 200/203/205) and refuses the other functions by name and block number.\n\nEffort: max\n\nRefs #2227\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n",
